{title: Shield Around Me}
{subtitle: Psalms 3:4–5}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Gm] [Eb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
LORD how ma[Eb]ny foes surround me [Bb]now
[Gm]Many [Eb]rise to bring me [Bb]down
They [Gm]say there is no [F]help for [Gm]me [Gm7]
[Eb]No hope in [F]God to be [Bb]seen
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But you [Eb]LORD are a [Bb]shield around [F]me
My [Eb]glory that [Bb]lifts my head [F]high
I call [Gm]aloud [Eb]to you in [Bb]need
You an[Eb]swer me from your [F]holy moun[Bb]tain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I lie down [Eb]and sleep in [Bb]peace [F/A]
[Gm]I wake a[Eb]gain sustained by [Bb]grace
[F/A]The [Gm]tens of thousands [F]on every [Gm]side [F]
[Eb]Cannot make [F]me fear your [Bb]ways
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But you [Eb]LORD are a [Bb]shield around [F]me
My [Eb]glory that [Bb]lifts my head [F]high
I call [Gm]aloud [Eb]to you in [Bb]need
You answer [Eb]me from your [F]holy moun[Bb]tain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Rise up [Eb]LORD and save me [Bb]now [F/A]
[Gm]My [Eb]God you strike the en[Bb]emies [F/A]
[Gm]You break [Eb]the teeth of the [Bb]wicked ones [F/A]
[Eb]And [F]bring them to their [Bb]end
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]You are [Bb]my shield and my [F]glory
[Eb]My head lift[Bb]ed high in your [F]light [Gm][Eb][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
